(30) ‘Horizontal Disallowance’ means a disallowance of offsets to required capital
used for assessing market risk for regulatory capital. In order to calculate the
capital required for interest rate risk of a trading book, offsetting of long and short
positions is permitted. However, interest rate risk of instruments at different
horizontal points of the yield curve are not perfectly correlated. Hence, this
method requires that a portion of these offsets be disallowed;

