Chapter-VIII Best Practices

45. A CIC shall take into account the following best practices:

(i)
have a structured and systematic process for redressing customer
grievance redressal;

(ii)
have a nodal officer for dealing with customer complaints;

(iii) following a dispute regarding a CIR, if it is established that the reason for
the dispute lies with the CIC itself or with the information provided by a
member CI to the CIC, the CIC may provide a free copy of the same type of
CIR to customer after correction of the credit information;

(iv) organise trainings for member CIs in order to make them understand the
formats, importance of data reporting and how to improve data acceptance
ratio;

(v)
build into agreements with the SUs, safeguards in respect of data usage in
terms of Rule 27 of the CIC Rules by SUs;

(vi) to avoid multiple financing for the same purpose / fraudulent transactions,
provide alerts to all CIs who have drawn reports whenever CIRs on the
same borrower are accessed by more than one CI within a period of one
month;

(vii) indicate to other credit grantors, without disclosing the name of the CIs,
alerts on borrowers who are changing their addresses / offices;

(viii) provide behaviour pattern of the borrowers, viz., frequency of loans
obtained, frequency of CIs approached etc. as a separate value-added
product;

(ix) customise reports as per the specific requirement of a SU as a separate
value-added product;

(x)
ensure that credit records of borrowers are regularly updated by CIs and
that issues such as non-reporting of repayment of the last instalment of a
loan do not arise;

(xi) be ISO 27001 certified for Information Security; and

